\tag{fdip}
\title{States and pullback of observables}
\date{2026-10-23}

\p{An observable algebra records which quantities can be added and
multiplied; a normalized linear functional assigns them expectation
values. A supplied algebra map pulls a functional back by
precomposition, preserving its value on the unit.}

\p{Coordinate restriction pulls polynomial functions back, so a
normalized functional on the larger polynomial algebra restricts to
the retained one. Gaussian measures, positivity and integrability
enter in [positive Gaussian laws](fdip-0017).
[Finite-state constructions](fdip-0040) give separate weight and
pushforward examples.}

